From e035a41e72f8b3183738fc9bbe23a89e31f8545c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "claude[bot]" <41898282+claude[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 03:15:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] Use Opentrons' P20 GEN2 plunger planes and pass
 microlitres through

The p20_single_gen2 entry was all placeholders, with two separate effects.

1. Volumes were converted twice. OpentronsPipette.aspirate/dispense/mix send
   volume_ul * mm_to_ul as the ASPIRATE argument, but the PANDA firmware's
   aspirate() takes microlitres and applies its own UL_TO_MM. A 20 uL request
   became 20 x 0.025 = 0.5, which the firmware clamped up to MIN_VOLUME and
   converted again. mm_to_ul = 1.0 makes this side a pass-through and leaves
   the single conversion in the firmware.

2. prime/blowout/drop_tip positions are absolute MOVE_TO targets, so the
   placeholders named the wrong destinations, not just the wrong scale. The
   values now come from Opentrons shared-data
   pipette/definitions/1/pipetteModelSpecs.json (p20_single_v2.0/2.1/2.2,
   identical in all three), converted from Opentrons' top-relative frame to
   CubOS's downward-from-home frame as top - field, with top = 19.5:

       prime_position     bottom  -8.5  ->  28.0  (was  5.0)
       blowout_position   blowout -13   ->  32.5  (was  7.0)
       drop_tip_position  dropTip -27   ->  46.5  (was 10.0)
       mm_to_ul                          ->   1.0  (was  0.025)

The ordering 0 < prime < blowout < drop_tip that aspirate/dispense/moveTo
rely on is preserved. These are Opentrons' figures for the model, not a
measurement of one unit, so they apply to anyone with a P20 GEN2. The
p300_single_gen2 entry also differs from Opentrons and is left alone here.

Deployed on the lab's CubXL Pi since 2026-09-17. Recorded in
vertical-cloud-lab/byu-vcl as cubos/patches/p20-gen2-plunger-constants.patch.
Candidate for upstream.

Co-authored-by: Sterling G. Baird <45469701+sgbaird@users.noreply.github.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../src/cubos/instruments/pipette/models.py   | 33 ++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 29 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/packages/core/src/cubos/instruments/pipette/models.py b/packages/core/src/cubos/instruments/pipette/models.py
index efde55e..4ff2b35 100644
--- a/packages/core/src/cubos/instruments/pipette/models.py
+++ b/packages/core/src/cubos/instruments/pipette/models.py
@@ -96,11 +96,36 @@ PIPETTE_MODELS: dict[str, PlungerPipetteConfig] = {
         channels=1,
         max_volume=20.0,
         min_volume=1.0,
+        # ── byu-vcl: P20 GEN2, from Opentrons shared-data ───────────────────
+        # Source: shared-data/pipette/definitions/1/pipetteModelSpecs.json,
+        # keys p20_single_v2.0/2.1/2.2 (all three carry identical positions).
+        # Opentrons states these as signed offsets in a frame whose `top` is
+        # the plunger home reference; CubOS and the PANDA firmware both
+        # measure distance DOWNWARD from home, so each value is
+        # (top - <opentrons field>) with top = 19.5:
+        #
+        #     bottom  -8.5  ->  prime_position     28.0   (was 5.0)
+        #     blowout -13   ->  blowout_position   32.5   (was 7.0)
+        #     dropTip -27   ->  drop_tip_position  46.5   (was 10.0)
+        #
+        # These are sent to the firmware as ABSOLUTE MOVE_TO targets, so the
+        # 5/7/10 placeholders did not merely mis-scale -- they aimed at the
+        # wrong planes entirely, ~23 to ~36 mm short of where a P20 GEN2
+        # plunger primes, blows out and ejects.  They now agree with
+        # include/Pipette.h in the VCL PANDA firmware, which carries the same
+        # three numbers; see cubos/firmware/README.md.
         zero_position=0.0,
-        prime_position=5.0,       # placeholder
-        blowout_position=7.0,     # placeholder
-        drop_tip_position=10.0,   # placeholder
-        mm_to_ul=0.025,           # placeholder
+        prime_position=28.0,
+        blowout_position=32.5,
+        drop_tip_position=46.5,
+        # byu-vcl: was 0.025 (placeholder).  aspirate/dispense/mix send
+        # volume_ul * mm_to_ul to the firmware as the ASPIRATE argument, but
+        # the PANDA firmware's aspirate(volume, ...) takes MICROLITRES and
+        # applies its own UL_TO_MM internally -- so the conversion was
+        # happening twice.  1.0 makes this side a pass-through and leaves the
+        # single conversion in the firmware, where the calibration constant
+        # lives (UL_TO_MM 1.34 for a P20 GEN2).
+        mm_to_ul=1.0,
     ),
     "p300_single_gen2": PlungerPipetteConfig(
         name="p300_single_gen2",
